Subject: [PATCH 09/14] =?UTF-8?q?grpc-stream:=20wallet2=20integration=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20pull=5Fblocks=20routes=20through=20gRPC=20stream=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?when=20endpoint=20is=20set?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 1c step 3 — the actual pull pipeline finally sees the stream.
Local Release build with MONERO_ENABLE_GRPC_STREAM=ON passes; default
OFF build path still compiles and behaves identically (no layout change,
no new code paths exercised).

How it works:
- New public API: wallet2::set_grpc_stream_endpoint("host:port"). Empty
  string disables. No-op against standard monerod nodes (they don't
  expose the gRPC endpoint) — safe default.
- pull_blocks() first tries try_pull_blocks_grpc(). On any failure
  (connect error, stream error, deser failure, end-of-stream, mismatched
  block/index lengths) it closes the stream and falls through to the
  existing bin RPC path for this iteration. Next refresh() opens a fresh
  stream from the new m_blockchain size.
- Chunk payloads are exactly the epee-serialized GetBlocksResponse the
  bin RPC produces, so we reuse epee::serialization::load_t_from_binary
  straight into a COMMAND_RPC_GET_BLOCKS_FAST::response — no new
  deserializer needed on the wallet side.
- The `first && !m_background_syncing` call is routed to bin RPC only
  (needs pool-info payload, which the streaming proto doesn't carry
  yet). Every subsequent call goes through the stream.
- pull_and_parse_next_blocks()'s speculative prefetch is disabled when
  the stream is active. The single gRPC stream IS the prefetch (server
  pushes continuously + HTTP/2 flow control gives natural backpressure),
  spawning 16 parallel bin-RPC prefetches would race against it and
  serve no purpose.
- m_grpc_stream_fallback_to_bin latches on permanent errors (connect
  failed, deser failed) so we don't thrash re-opening a dead stream each
  call. Set_grpc_stream_endpoint clears the latch.

ABI note: MONERO_GRPC_STREAM moved from PRIVATE to PUBLIC compile
definition on the wallet target — wallet2's class layout differs
depending on the #ifdef, so downstream TUs (wallet_rpc_server,
simplewallet, monero-wallet-gui) must observe the same flag to stay
ABI-compatible.

Not tested end-to-end against a deployed cuprated in this commit; the
standalone cuprate_grpc_stream_test binary already validated the client
+ server do talk correctly. End-to-end wallet sync test is the next
step — expecting a big jump vs. the 16-parallel bin RPC baseline
(standalone C++ client already hit 22.7 MB/s sustained streaming on
one connection, beating the 16-parallel bin setup's 12.6 MB/s aggregate).
